## 🤖 Copy-Paste Master AI Prompt

Use the prompt below in code generators (like v0, Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or Gemini) to rebuild the dashboard.

````markdown
# TASK: Build a Premium, Highly Interactive SaaS Dashboard UI in React / Next.js / Tailwind CSS

Create a professional, production-grade, state-of-the-art SaaS admin dashboard with a modern minimalist aesthetic, collapsible sidebar navigation, responsive layout containers, KPI metric cards, an interactive double-gradient area chart, and a highly functional data table with drag-and-drop ordering and inline-editable cells.

## 1. Technical Stack & Dependencies
Ensure the implementation uses the following:
- **Core Framework**: React (with React Hooks) / Next.js (App Router structure).
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v3 (using CSS variables for color tokens) and `clsx` / `tailwind-merge` utilities.
- **Icons**: Lucide React or Tabler Icons (`@tabler/icons-react`).
- **Charts**: Recharts.
- **Table System**: `@tanstack/react-table` combined with `@dnd-kit/core` and `@dnd-kit/sortable` for vertical drag-and-drop row reordering.
- **Toasts & Feedback**: `sonner` for status notifications.
- **Validation**: Zod (for row schema definition).
- **Responsive container queries**: Tailwind plugin `@tailwindcss/container-queries`.

---

## 2. Design System & Global Styles
Configure HSL color variables inside a global CSS file (`globals.css` style) to support light/dark modes:
- Default Light Mode background is a clean off-white. The Sidebar background is a light neutral (`hsl(0 0% 98%)`), with standard card backgrounds set to pure white.
- Border colors: Light gray border color (`hsl(0 0% 89.8%)`).
- Border-radius values: Base radius variable set to `0.5rem` (`--radius: 0.5rem`), with sub-radii scaling down (`calc(var(--radius) - 2px)`).
- Inject CSS variables to handle the layout grid dynamically:
  - `--sidebar-width: 18rem;`
  - `--header-height: 3rem;`

---

## 3. Core Page Layout & Sidebar
- **Layout wrapper**: Wrap the dashboard structure inside a `<SidebarProvider>` layout.
- **App Sidebar (`AppSidebar`)**: 
  - An `inset` variant sidebar that collapses offcanvas on mobile.
  - Header: Acme Inc branding (logo placeholder + semibold header).
  - Main Navigation: Main list (Dashboard, Lifecycle, Analytics, Projects, Team) with accompanying icons.
  - Collapsible Groups: Collapsible sub-navigation drawers (e.g., Capture, Proposal, Prompts) each nesting child links (e.g., Active Proposals, Archived).
  - Documents section: Pinned links (Data Library, Reports, Word Assistant).
  - Pinned footer actions: Settings, Help, Search, and a custom User profile button dropdown displaying user avatar, name, email, and actions.
- **Site Header (`SiteHeader`)**:
  - Sticky header (`h-12`) with a sidebar toggle trigger button, vertical separator, page title ("Documents"), and a right-aligned utility action button.
- **Main Container**: `<SidebarInset>` containing the layout. Use a container-query wrapper on the main element (`@container/main`).

---

## 4. KPI Section Cards (`SectionCards`)
Create a grid block that auto-arranges based on container widths (1 column to 4 columns max):
- Use styling `grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 @xl/main:grid-cols-2 @5xl/main:grid-cols-4 px-4 lg:px-6`.
- Cards must use a subtle bottom-to-top gradient background: `bg-gradient-to-t from-primary/5 to-card shadow-xs`.
- **Card 1 (Total Revenue)**: Value `$1,250.00` in tabular digits. A trend badge containing a green up-trending arrow and `+12.5%`. Footer description: "Trending up this month" + details.
- **Card 2 (New Customers)**: Value `1,234`. Trend badge showing `-20%` (red down-trending arrow). Footer description: "Down 20% this period".
- **Card 3 (Active Accounts)**: Value `45,678`. Trend badge showing `+12.5%`. Footer description: "Strong user retention".
- **Card 4 (Growth Rate)**: Value `4.5%`. Trend badge showing `+4.5%`. Footer description: "Steady performance increase".

---

## 5. Interactive Area Chart Component (`ChartAreaInteractive`)
- **Container**: An elegant white card with Title "Total Visitors" and responsive description text.
- **Controls (Header Actions)**: 
  - Use a container query breakpoint (`@[767px]/card`). On wide screens, display an outline `<ToggleGroup>` offering options: `Last 3 months`, `Last 30 days`, `Last 7 days`.
  - On narrow screens, dynamically collapse this toggle group and hide it, rendering a native `<Select>` dropdown instead.
- **Chart Visuals**:
  - Render an interactive, stacked `<AreaChart>` using Recharts.
  - Define linear gradients: `fillDesktop` and `fillMobile`.
  - Configure the chart area to hide vertical grid lines, keeping only horizontal ones.
  - Include an interactive hover tooltip component (`ChartTooltip` using `<ChartTooltipContent indicator="dot" />`) displaying exact statistics when hovering.

---

## 6. Premium Interactive Data Table (`DataTable`)
Implement a comprehensive TanStack Table containing advanced interactivity:
- **Upper Navigation Bar**:
  - Swappable views: Segmented `<TabsList>` showing `Outline`, `Past Performance (count badge: 3)`, `Key Personnel (count badge: 2)`, `Focus Documents`.
  - Responsive collapse: On screen sizes below `@4xl/main`, collapse the tabs list into a Select menu switcher.
  - Right-aligned actions: 
    - "Customize Columns" dropdown menu mapping checkboxes to visible columns (`table.getAllColumns()`).
    - "Add Section" primary trigger button.
- **Table Data Grid**:
  - The table body must be enclosed in a drag-and-drop context (`<DndContext>` and `<SortableContext>`) using `@dnd-kit/sortable` to support drag reordering.
  - Column 1: Vertical grab handle grip icon that acts as the sortable drag handle activator.
  - Column 2: Selection checkbox for rows and headers (supporting indeterminate select).
  - Column 3 (Header Title): Styled as a click-trigger link button. When clicked, it must slide in a details Drawer sheet (Drawer component shifts direction: slides in from the `right` on desktop, and from the `bottom` on mobile views).
    - Inside the Drawer: Display a mini Recharts area chart of past data, separated by styled dividers, followed by input forms (header, type selector, status selector, target/limit fields, reviewer picker).
  - Column 4 (Section Type): Rendered in a clean outline `<Badge>`.
  - Column 5 (Status): Displays status value with a checkmark badge (if "Done", render a solid green checkmark icon; otherwise, render a gray loading spinner icon).
  - Column 6 & 7 (Target and Limit): Inline editable text input fields. The border is transparent by default and becomes visible on hover/focus. When editing a value and submitting the form (hitting Enter), trigger a simulated loading promise via `sonner` (`toast.promise`) showing "Saving [item]" followed by a "Done" feedback toast.
  - Column 8 (Reviewer): Renders the assigned name or, if unassigned, renders a responsive Select dropdown menu inline to assign the reviewer.
  - Column 9 (Actions menu): Triple-dot vertical dropdown menu listing "Edit", "Make a copy", "Favorite", and a separator before a red "Delete" action.
- **Footer Pagination Section**:
  - Left: "X of Y rows selected" text.
  - Right: Page size rows-per-page dropdown selection list (`[10, 20, 30, 40, 50]`), current page indicator status ("Page A of B"), and navigation icons (first page `<<`, previous page `<`, next page `>`, last page `>>`).
